hould not simply be crowded into Wednesday morning instead.","answerKey":"C","rubric":null,"sourceMaterial":null,"responseConstraints":null,"primaryEvidence":null,"taskletPosition":4,"bankVersion":"pilot-0.5","qualityStatus":"approved_for_pilot","psychometricStatus":"uncalibrated"},{"externalId":"L-B2-002-Q1","level":"B2","skill":"listening","category":"Listening","topic":"environment","genre":"radio_interview","audience":"general","taskletExternalId":"L-B2-002","subskill":"speaker_attitude","difficulty":4,"taskType":"multiple_choice","questionType":"listening","prompt":"What misconception does Priya identify?","options":["Urban residents generally dislike seeing birds and insects in parks.","A neat-looking park is necessarily an ecologically healthier park.","Fungi prevent dead wood from supporting other forms of wildlife.","Fallen trees are more dangerous than standing trees in every situation."],"answer":"A neat-looking park is necessarily an ecologically healthier park.","answerKey":"B","rubric":null,"sourceMaterial":null,"responseConstraints":null,"primaryEvidence":null,"taskletPosition":1,"bankVersion":"pilot-0.5","qualityStatus":"approved_for_pilot","psychometricStatus":"uncalibrated"},{"externalId":"L-B2-002-Q2","level":"B2","skill":"listening","category":"Listening","topic":"environment","genre":"radio_interview","audience":"general","taskletExternalId":"L-B2-002","subskill":"inference","difficulty":4,"taskType":"multiple_choice","questionType":"listening","prompt":"Why does Priya reject the idea of leaving every fallen tree?","options":["Residents should decide individually which trees are removed.","Only trees in large forests can provide useful habitats.","Dead trees stop supporting wildlife when they are close to paths.","Ecological benefits must be weighed against safety and access."],"answer":"Ecological benefits must be weighed against safety and access.","answerKey":"D","rubric":null,"sourceMaterial":null,"responseConstraints":null,"primaryEvidence"