w","audience":"adult","taskletExternalId":"L-C1-001","subskill":"nuanced_stance","difficulty":5,"taskType":"multiple_choice","questionType":"listening","prompt":"What is Professor Wu''s position on using metrics to assess collaboration?","options":["They are useful alongside context and other evidence, but are not direct measures of it.","They are more reliable than managerial judgement because they reduce subjective interpretation.","They are useful mainly for identifying employees who deliberately manipulate performance systems.","They should be abandoned because numerical measures inevitably distort how employees collaborate."],"answer":"They are useful alongside context and other evidence, but are not direct measures of it.","answerKey":"A","rubric":null,"sourceMaterial":null,"responseConstraints":null,"primaryEvidence":null,"taskletPosition":1,"bankVersion":"pilot-0.5","qualityStatus":"approved_for_pilot","psychometricStatus":"uncalibrated"},{"externalId":"L-C1-001-Q2","level":"C1","skill":"listening","category":"Listening","topic":"work","genre":"expert_interview","audience":"adult","taskletExternalId":"L-C1-001","subskill":"implicit_meaning","difficulty":5,"taskType":"multiple_choice","questionType":"listening","prompt":"What does Wu mean when she says a measure can become ''a target''?","options":["People may change their behaviour to improve the measured number, not the real outcome.","Employees may refuse to collaborate if they know their activity is being recorded.","Managers may set an official minimum number of meetings for every employee.","A metric becomes useful only after the organisation publishes a numerical goal."],"answer":"People may change their behaviour to improve the measured number, not the real outcome.","answerKey":"A","rubric":null,"sourceMaterial":null,"responseConstraints":null,"primaryEvidence":null,"taskletPosition":2,"bankVersion":"pilot-0.5","qualityStatus":"approved_for_pilot","psychometricStatus":"uncalibrated"},{"externalId":"L